        <dictScrap type="liebermann"><hi rend="bold">hlafætan</hi>, <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:accusativus"><abbr>ac</abbr></ref>, Brotesser, Kostgänger</hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Abt">Abt</ref> 25 [<hi rend="italic">‘Brot’ <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:fur"><abbr>für</abbr></ref> ‘Haushaltsgenuss’ <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:auch"><abbr>auch</abbr></ref> im <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:frankisch"><abbr>Fränk.</abbr></ref> Stadtrecht des späteren Mittelalters: ‘der Vater scheidet <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:vor"><abbr>vor</abbr></ref> Gericht den Sohn <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:aus"><abbr>aus</abbr></ref> seinem Brote, <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:dasHeisst"><abbr>d. h.</abbr></ref> macht wirtschaftlich selbständig’:</hi> exseparat, emancipat, forisfamiliat; <ref type="bibl" target="bib:CitBrunnerEnc"><hi rend="italic">Brunner in</hi> Encycl. Rechtswiss. (1902) <hi rend="italic">S.</hi> 256</ref>. <hi rend="italic">‘Brotessend’ <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:friesisch"><abbr>fris.</abbr></ref> <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:fur"><abbr>für</abbr></ref> ‘freies Gesinde’: </hi><ref type="bibl" target="bib:CitHisSF"><hi rend="italic">His</hi> Strafr. d. Friesen 50</ref>]</dictScrap>
